Rule 1 (mask rank must not exceed data rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≤ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (mask must be boolean)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 3 (mask shape must be a prefix of data shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 4 (2D mask with 2D data: dimensions must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, 0) ∧ shape(v_2, 1) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 5 (4D mask with 4D data: all leading dimensions must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 6 (3D mask applied to 6D data must match leading dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 6 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 2] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 7 (row-wise mask for 2D data)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, 0)
